# Cloud Brain — environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the two values from your Supabase
# project. `.env` is gitignored; this template is committed so the required
# variables are discoverable without sharing any secrets.
#
# WHERE TO FIND THESE
#   Supabase dashboard -> your project -> Settings -> API Keys
#
# WHICH KEY
#   Use the PUBLISHABLE key (starts `sb_publishable_...`) if your project has
#   one. If you only see Legacy API Keys, use the `anon` / `public` key (a long
#   JWT starting `eyJ...`). They behave identically for this app; Supabase is
#   retiring the legacy naming.
#
# THE EXPO_PUBLIC_ PREFIX IS DELIBERATE
#   It tells Metro to inline the value into the JavaScript bundle. Both values
#   below are designed to be public and shipped inside the APK — the anon /
#   publishable key is safe because Row Level Security restricts what it can
#   reach (see supabase/migrations/0002_rls_policies.sql, verified by
#   `npm run verify:rls`).
#
# NEVER PUT THESE HERE
#   - the `service_role` or `secret` key  -> bypasses ALL security
#   - the database password               -> full Postgres access
#   Anything with EXPO_PUBLIC_ ends up in the APK, where it is extractable.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste-your-publishable-or-anon-key-here
